# Scaling study: 100 MHz, 30 kHz SCS, Cat-B precoding [MEASURED] H100 compute-only
Device: NVIDIA H100 NVL; CPU core 10; FFTW + AVX-512 BFP; slot=0.5 ms
Production OCUDU call site: resource_grid_mapper_impl.cpp:245-263
  (pre-stored get_prg_coefficients + apply_precoding on RE views).
Timed CPU path: AVX-512 strip over REs with per-PRB weights — same kernel math as
  channel_precoder_avx512.cpp:221-269 (apply_precoding_port), for ALL port counts.
  (Calling OCUDU apply_precoding once per Cat-B PRB of 12 REs cannot amortize AVX;
   that pattern is still exercised for fidelity and reported as ocudu_prg_p50.)
Scalar reference (channel_precoder_generic.cpp:9-30) is correctness-only.
Pass tolerance: max |gpu-cpu| after bf16→float ≤ 1e-03 (mismatch tripwire 1e-05 is diagnostic).
GPU precoding: custom CUDA Cat-B kernel; Jetson not claimed

